# Project Structure and Architecture

## Architecture Overview

This project follows **Clean Architecture** with **MVVM** pattern:

- **Domain Layer** (`domain/`): Business logic, entities, use cases, repository interfaces
- **Data Layer** (`data/`): Repository implementations, data sources (local/remote), DTOs
- **Presentation Layer** (`presentation/`): UI components, ViewModels, screens, navigation

## Directory Structure

```
app/src/main/java/com/example/baseapp/
├── core/                          # Core functionality
│   ├── di/                        # Dependency injection modules
│   ├── network/                   # Network utilities
│   ├── database/                  # Database configuration
│   └── util/                      # Utility classes
├── data/                          # Data layer
│   ├── local/                     # Local data sources (Room)
│   ├── remote/                    # Remote data sources (Retrofit)
│   ├── model/                     # DTOs and Entities
│   └── repository/                # Repository implementations
├── domain/                        # Domain layer
│   ├── model/                     # Domain models
│   ├── repository/                # Repository interfaces
│   └── usecase/                   # Use cases
└── presentation/                  # Presentation layer
    ├── components/                # Reusable UI components
    ├── features/                  # Feature modules
    ├── navigation/                # Navigation logic
    ├── theme/                     # Theme and styling
    └── util/                      # Presentation utilities
```

## Key Files

- Main entry: [MainActivity.kt](mdc:app/src/main/java/com/example/baseapp/MainActivity.kt)
- Application: [MyApplication.kt](mdc:app/src/main/java/com/example/baseapp/MyApplication.kt)
- Dependencies: [libs.versions.toml](mdc:gradle/libs.versions.toml)
- Build configuration: [build.gradle.kts](mdc:app/build.gradle.kts)

## Technology Stack

- **UI**: Jetpack Compose with Material 3
- **Navigation**: Voyager
- **DI**: Hilt
- **Network**: Retrofit + Gson
- **Database**: Room
- **Async**: Kotlin Coroutines + Flow
- **Testing**: JUnit, MockK, Compose Test, Turbine

## Architecture Principles

1. **Separation of Concerns**: Each layer has distinct responsibilities
2. **Dependency Rule**: Dependencies point inward (presentation → domain ← data)
3. **Single Responsibility**: Each class has one reason to change
4. **Testability**: All layers are independently testable
5. **Reactive**: Use Flow for data streams
6. **Responsive**: Support multiple screen sizes (phones, tablets, foldables)